/-!
# The quasi-coherent subalgebra generated by a quasi-coherent submodule

Let `X` be a scheme and `A` a quasi-coherent sheaf of commutative `𝒪_X`-algebras.  Given a
concrete quasi-coherent submodule `M` of the underlying `𝒪_X`-module of `A`, this file builds the
**subalgebra of `A` generated by `M`**: over an affine open `U` its sections are
`Algebra.adjoin Γ(X, U) (M(U))`, and over an arbitrary open they are the sections of `A` whose
restriction to every affine open inside lies in that subalgebra.  It is quasi-coherent, and of
finite type as soon as `M` is.

On a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme every section of `A` over an affine open comes from
a finite type quasi-coherent subalgebra of `A` on the whole of `X`.

## Main definitions

* `adjoinSubmodule A U s`: the `Γ(X, U)`-subalgebra of the sections of `A` over `U` generated by
  a set `s` of sections, read as a `Γ(X, U)`-submodule of the sections of the underlying module.
* `genFamily A M`: that subalgebra at `s = M(U)`, as a family indexed by the affine opens.
* `genSubalg A M hM`: the family glued into a
  `Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf.Subalg A`, i.e. a subring of the sections of `A` over every
  open, containing the image of `𝒪_X`, stable under restriction and local.

## Main results

* `isCompatible_sections`: the sections of a quasi-coherent submodule of a quasi-coherent module
  form a compatible family in the sense of
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.IsCompatible`.
* `adjoin_toSubmodule_eq_span_image`: a generated subalgebra base-changes to a generated
  subalgebra.
* `isCompatible_adjoinSubmodule`: the subalgebras generated by a compatible family of submodules
  form a compatible family.
* `exists_submodule_mem_of_qcqs`: on a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme, a section of a
  quasi-coherent module over an affine open lies in a finite type quasi-coherent submodule.
* `isQuasicoherent_genSubalg` and `isFiniteType_genSubalg`: the generated subalgebra is
  quasi-coherent, and of finite type when `M` is.
* `exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section`: on a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme, every
  section of `A` over an affine open comes from a finite type quasi-coherent subalgebra.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05JT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05JT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0817](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0817)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01I9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01I9)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PB)
-/

